(7) Tj T*
(it to handle complex, multi-step tasks that a model alone cannot. The critical capability is that) Tj T*
(agents can work on their own, figuring out the next steps needed to reach a goal without a) Tj T*
(person guiding them at every turn.) Tj T*
(This document is the first in a five-part series, acting as a formal guide for the developers,) Tj T*
(architects, and product leaders transitioning from proofs-of-concept to robust,) Tj T*
(production-grade agentic systems. While building a simple prototype is straightforward,) Tj T*
(ensuring security, quality and reliability is a significant challenge. This paper provides a) Tj T*
(comprehensive foundation:) Tj T*
(* Core Anatomy: Deconstructing an agent into its three essential components: the) Tj T*
(reasoning Model, actionable Tools, and the governing Orchestration Layer.) Tj T*
(* A Taxonomy of Capabilities: Classifying agents from simple, connected problem-solvers) Tj T*
(to complex, collaborative multi-agent systems.) Tj T*
(* Architectural Design: Diving into the practical design considerations for each) Tj T*
(component, from model selection to tool implementation.) Tj T*
(* Building for Production: Establishing the Agent Ops discipline needed to evaluate,) Tj T*
(debug, secure, and scale agentic systems from a single instance to a fleet with) Tj T*
(enterprise governance.) Tj T*
(Building on the previous Agents whitepaper1 and Agent Companion2; this guide provides) Tj T*
(the foundational concepts and strategic frameworks you will need to successfully build,) Tj T*
(deploy, and manage this new generation of intelligent applications which can reason, act and) Tj T*
(observe to accomplish goals3.) Tj T*
ET
