(Page 8 of 54 - 01 - Introduction  to Agents) Tj T*
(Introduction to Agents) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(8) Tj T*
(Words are insufficient to describe how humans interact with AI. We tend to) Tj T*
(anthropomorphize and use human terms like "think" and "reason" and "know." We don't) Tj T*
(yet have words for "know with semantic meaning" vs "know with high probability of) Tj T*
(maximizing a reward function." Those are two different types of knowing, but the results) Tj T*
(are the same 99.X% of the time.) Tj T*
(Introduction to AI Agents) Tj T*
(In the simplest terms, an AI Agent can be defined as the combination of models, tools, an) Tj T*
(orchestration layer, and runtime services which uses the LM in a loop to accomplish a goal.) Tj T*
(These four elements form the essential architecture of any autonomous system.) Tj T*
(* The Model \(The "Brain"\): The core language model \(LM\) or foundation model that serves) Tj T*
(as the agent's central reasoning engine to process information, evaluate options, and) Tj T*
(make decisions. The type of model \(general-purpose, fine-tuned, or multimodal\) dictates) Tj T*
(the agent's cognitive capabilities.  An agentic system is the ultimate curator of the input) Tj T*
(context window the LM.) Tj T*
(* Tools \(The "Hands"\): These mechanisms connect the agent's reasoning to the outside) Tj T*
(world, enabling actions beyond text generation. They include API extensions, code) Tj T*
(functions, and data stores \(like databases or vector stores\) for accessing real-time, factual) Tj T*
(information.  An agentic system allows a LM to plan which tools to use, executes the tool,) Tj T*
(and puts the tool results into the  input context window of the next LM call.) Tj T*
(* The Orchestration Layer \(The "Nervous System"\): The governing process that) Tj T*
(manages the agent's operational loop. It handles planning, memory \(state\), and reasoning) Tj T*
(strategy execution. This layer uses prompting frameworks and reasoning techniques \(like) Tj T*
ET
endstream
