(9) Tj T*
(Chain-of-Thought4 or ReAct5\) to break down complex goals into steps and decide when) Tj T*
(to think versus use a tool. This layer is also responsible for giving agents the memory) Tj T*
(to "remember.") Tj T*
(* Deployment \(The "Body and Legs"\): While building an agent on a laptop is effective for) Tj T*
(prototyping, production deployment is what makes it a reliable and accessible service.) Tj T*
(This involves hosting the agent on a secure, scalable server and integrating it with) Tj T*
(essential production services for monitoring, logging, and management. Once deployed,) Tj T*
(the agent can be accessed by users through a graphical interface or programmatically by) Tj T*
(other agents via an Agent-to-Agent \(A2A\) API.) Tj T*
(At the end of the day, building a generative AI agent is a new way to develop solutions to) Tj T*
(solve tasks. The traditional developer acts as a "bricklayer," precisely defining every logical) Tj T*
(step. The agent developer, in contrast, is more like a director. Instead of writing explicit code) Tj T*
(for every action, you set the scene \(the guiding instructions and prompts\), select the cast) Tj T*
(\(the tools and APIs\), and provide the necessary context \(the data\). The primary task becomes) Tj T*
(guiding this autonomous "actor" to deliver the intended performance.) Tj T*
(You'll quickly find that an LM's greatest strength--its incredible flexibility--is also your biggest) Tj T*
(headache. A large language model's capacity to do anything makes it difficult to compel it to) Tj T*
(do one specific thing reliably and perfectly. What we used to call "prompt engineering" and) Tj T*
(now call "context engineering" guides LMs to generate the desired output. For any single) Tj T*
(call to a LM, we input our instructions, facts, available tools to call, examples, session history,) Tj T*
(user profile, etc - filling the context window with just the right information to get the outputs) Tj T*
(we need. Agents are software which manage the inputs of LMs to get work done.) Tj T*
(Debugging becomes essential when issues arise. "Agent Ops" essentially redefines the) Tj T*
(familiar cycle of measurement, analysis, and system optimization. Through traces and logs,) Tj T*
(you can monitor the agent's "thought process" to identify deviations from the intended) Tj T*
(execution path. As models evolve and frameworks improve, the developer's role is to furnish) Tj T*
