(Page 13 of 54 - 01 - Introduction  to Agents) Tj T*
(Introduction to Agents) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(13) Tj T*
(Instead of immediately acting, the agent first enters its "Think It Through" phase to devise a) Tj T*
(complete strategy. It reasons:) Tj T*
("The user wants a delivery status. To provide a complete answer, I need a multi-step plan:) Tj T*
(1. Identify: I must first find the order in our internal database to confirm it exists and get) Tj T*
(its details.) Tj T*
(2. Track: From those details, I'll need to extract the shipping carrier's tracking number. Then,) Tj T*
(I'll query the external carrier's API for the live status.) Tj T*
(3. Report: Finally, I must synthesize the information I've gathered into a clear, helpful) Tj T*
(response for the user.") Tj T*
(With this multi-step plan in mind, the agent begins execution.) Tj T*
(In its first "Act" phase, it executes step one of its plan, calling the find_order\("12345"\)) Tj T*
(tool. It observes the result--a full order record, including the tracking number "ZYX987.") Tj T*
(The agent's orchestration layer recognizes that the first part of its plan is complete) Tj T*
(and immediately proceeds to the second. It acts by calling the get_shipping_) Tj T*
(status\("ZYX987"\) tool. It observes the new result: "Out for Delivery.") Tj T*
(Finally, having successfully executed the data-gathering stages of its plan, the agent) Tj T*
(moves to the "Report" step. It perceives it has all the necessary components, plans the final) Tj T*
(message, and acts by generating the response: "Your order #12345 is 'Out for Delivery'!) Tj T*
ET
endstream
