(Page 16 of 54 - 01 - Introduction  to Agents) Tj T*
(Introduction to Agents) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(16) Tj T*
(This fundamental ability to interact with the world - whether using a search tool for a score ,) Tj T*
(a financial API for a live stock price, or a database via Retrieval-Augmented Generation \(RAG\)) Tj T*
(is the core capability of a Level 1 agent.) Tj T*
(Level 2: The Strategic Problem-Solver) Tj T*
(Level 2 marks a significant expansion in capability, moving from executing simple tasks to) Tj T*
(strategically planning complex, multi-part goals. The key skill that emerges here is context) Tj T*
(engineering: the agent's ability to actively select, package, and manage the most relevant) Tj T*
(information for each step of its plan.) Tj T*
(An agent's accuracy depends on a focused, high-quality context. Context engineering) Tj T*
(curates the model's limited attention to prevent overload and ensure efficient performance.) Tj T*
(For instance, consider the "Mission": "Find a good coffee shop halfway between my office) Tj T*
(at 1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, and my client's office at 1 Market St,) Tj T*
(San Francisco.") Tj T*
(A Level 2 agent will start creating a plan:) Tj T*
(1. Think: "I must first find the halfway point.") Tj T*
(* Act: Call the Maps tool with both addresses.) Tj T*
(* Observe: "The halfway point is Millbrae, CA.") Tj T*
(2. Think: "Now I must find coffee shops in Millbrae. The user asked for 'good' ones, so I will) Tj T*
(search for places with a 4-star rating or higher.") Tj T*
ET
