(3. Delegates to WebDevAgent: "Generate the new product page HTML based on the) Tj T*
(attached design mockups.") Tj T*
(This collaborative model, while currently constrained by the reasoning limitations of today's) Tj T*
(LMs, represents the frontier of automating entire, complex business workflows from start) Tj T*
(to finish.) Tj T*
(Level 4: The Self-Evolving System) Tj T*
(Level 4 represents a profound leap from delegation to autonomous creation and adaptation.) Tj T*
(At this level, an agentic system can identify gaps in its own capabilities and dynamically) Tj T*
(create new tools or even new agents to fill them. It moves from using a fixed set of resources) Tj T*
(to actively expanding them.) Tj T*
(Following our example, the "Project Manager" agent, tasked with the 'Solaris' launch, might) Tj T*
(realize it needs to monitor social media sentiment, but no such tool or agent exists on) Tj T*
(its team.) Tj T*
(1. Think \(Meta-Reasoning\): "I must track social media buzz for 'Solaris,' but I lack) Tj T*
(the capability.") Tj T*
(2. Act \(Autonomous Creation\): Instead of failing, it invokes a high-level AgentCreator tool) Tj T*
(with a new mission: "Build a new agent that monitors social media for keywords 'Solaris) Tj T*
(headphones', performs sentiment analysis, and reports a daily summary.") Tj T*
(3. Observe: A new, specialized SentimentAnalysisAgent is created, tested, and added to the) Tj T*
(team on the fly, ready to contribute to the original mission.) Tj T*
(This level of autonomy, where a system can dynamically expand its own capabilities, turns a) Tj T*
(team of agents into a truly learning and evolving organization.) Tj T*
ET
