(Introduction to Agents) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(21) Tj T*
(Here are a few of the main types of tools agent builders will put into the "hands" of) Tj T*
(their agents.  For a more complete deep dive see the agent tools focused whitepaper in) Tj T*
(this series.) Tj T*
(Retrieving Information: Grounding in Reality) Tj T*
(The most foundational tool is the ability to access up-to-date information. Retrieval-) Tj T*
(Augmented Generation \(RAG\) gives the agent a "library card" to query external knowledge,) Tj T*
(often stored in Vector Databases or Knowledge Graphs, ranging from internal company) Tj T*
(documents to web knowledge via Google Search. For structured data, Natural Language to) Tj T*
(SQL \(NL2SQL\) tools allow the agent to query databases to answer analytic questions like,) Tj T*
("What were our top-selling products last quarter?" By looking things up before speaking--) Tj T*
(whether in a document or a database--the agent grounds itself in fact, dramatically) Tj T*
(reducing hallucinations.) Tj T*
(Executing Actions: Changing the World) Tj T*
(The true power of agents is unleashed when they move from reading information to actively) Tj T*
(doing things. By wrapping existing APIs and code functions as tools, an agent can send an) Tj T*
(email, schedule a meeting, or update a customer record in ServiceNow. For more dynamic) Tj T*
(tasks, an agent can write and execute code on the fly. In a secure sandbox, it can generate) Tj T*
(a SQL query or a Python script to solve a complex problem or perform a calculation,) Tj T*
(transforming it from a knowledgeable assistant into an autonomous actor14.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
