(in the  instructions are usually very effective.) Tj T*
(Augment with Context) Tj T*
(The agent's "memory" is orchestrated into the LM context window at runtime. For a more) Tj T*
(complete deep dive see the agent memory focused whitepaper in this series.) Tj T*
(Short-term memory is the agent's active "scratchpad," maintaining the running history of the) Tj T*
(current conversation. It tracks the sequence of \(Action, Observation\) pairs from the ongoing) Tj T*
(loop, providing the immediate context the model needs to decide what to do next.  This may) Tj T*
(be implemented as abstractions like state, artifacts, sessions or threads.) Tj T*
(Long-term memory provides persistence across sessions. Architecturally, this is almost) Tj T*
(always implemented as another specialized tool--a RAG system connected to a vector) Tj T*
(database or search engine. The orchestrator gives the agent the ability to pre-fetch and to) Tj T*
(actively query its own history, allowing it to "remember" a user's preferences or the outcome) Tj T*
(of a similar task from weeks ago for a truly personalized and continuous experience.19) Tj T*
(Multi-Agent Systems and Design Patterns) Tj T*
(As tasks grow in complexity, building a single, all-powerful "super-agent" becomes inefficient.) Tj T*
(The more effective solution is to adopt a "team of specialists" approach, which mirrors) Tj T*
(a human organization. This is the core of a multi-agent system: a complex process is) Tj T*
ET
