(25) Tj T*
(segmented into discrete sub-tasks, and each is assigned to a dedicated, specialized AI agent.) Tj T*
(This division of labor allows each agent to be simpler, more focused, and easier to build, test,) Tj T*
(and maintain, which is ideal for dynamic or long-running business processes.) Tj T*
(Architects may rely on proven agentic design patterns, though agent capabilities and thus) Tj T*
(patterns are evolving rapidly.20 For dynamic or non-linear tasks, the Coordinator pattern is) Tj T*
(essential. It introduces a "manager" agent that analyzes a complex request, segments the) Tj T*
(primary task, and intelligently routes each sub-task to the appropriate specialist agent \(like a) Tj T*
(researcher, a writer, or a coder\). The coordinator then aggregates the responses from each) Tj T*
(specialist to formulate a final, comprehensive answer.) Tj T*
(Figure 3: The "iterative refinement" pattern from) Tj T*
(https://cloud.google.com/architecture/choose-design-pattern-agentic-ai-system) Tj T*
(For more linear workflows, the Sequential pattern is a better fit, acting like a digital assembly) Tj T*
(line where the output from one agent becomes the direct input for the next. Other key) Tj T*
(patterns focus on quality and safety. The Iterative Refinement pattern creates a feedback) Tj T*
(loop, using a "generator" agent to create content and a "critic" agent to evaluate it against) Tj T*
