(Agent Deployment and Services) Tj T*
(After you have built a local agent, you will want to deploy it to a server where it runs all the) Tj T*
(time and where other people and agents can use it.  Continuing our analogy, deployment and) Tj T*
(services would be the body and legs for our agent.  An agent requires several services to be) Tj T*
(effective, session history and memory persistence, and more.  As an agent builder, you will) Tj T*
(also be responsible for deciding what you log, and what security measures you take for data) Tj T*
(privacy and data residency and regulation compliance. All of these services are in scope,) Tj T*
(when deploying agents to production.) Tj T*
(Luckily, builders can rely on the newly launched Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform, which) Tj T*
(provides a single destination for technical teams to build, scale, govern, and optimize agents.) Tj T*
(This includes the new Agent Studio for seamless transitions from prompting to deployment,) Tj T*
(and a revamped Agent Runtime delivering sub-second cold starts, support for autonomous) Tj T*
(multi-day workflows, and Memory Bank for persistent long-term context across) Tj T*
(sessions, everything else one platform21.  For software developers who want to control their) Tj T*
(application stacks more directly, or deploy agents within their existing DevOps infrastructure,) Tj T*
(any agent and most agent services can be added to a docker container and deployed onto) Tj T*
(industry standard runtimes like Cloud Run or GKE22.) Tj T*
ET
