(Page 28 of 54 - 01 - Introduction  to Agents) Tj T*
(Introduction to Agents) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(28) Tj T*
(The transition from traditional, deterministic software to stochastic, agentic systems requires) Tj T*
(a new operational philosophy. Traditional software unit tests could simply assert output ==) Tj T*
(expected; but that doesn't work when an agent's response is probabilistic by design. Also,) Tj T*
(because language is complicated, it usually requires a LM to evaluate "quality" - that the) Tj T*
(agent's response does all of what it should, nothing it shouldn't, and with proper tone.) Tj T*
(Figure 5: Relationships between the operational domains of DevOps, MLOps, and GenAIOps from) Tj T*
(https://medium.com/@sokratis.kartakis/genai-in-production-mlops-or-genaiops-25691c9becd0) Tj T*
(Agent Ops is the disciplined, structured approach to managing this new reality. It is a natural) Tj T*
(evolution of DevOps and MLOps, tailored for the unique challenges of building, deploying,) Tj T*
(and governing AI agents, turning unpredictability from a liability into a managed, measurable,) Tj T*
(and reliable feature.24 For a more complete deep dive see the agent quality focused) Tj T*
(whitepaper in this series.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
