(Page 29 of 54 - 01 - Introduction  to Agents) Tj T*
(Introduction to Agents) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(29) Tj T*
(Measure What Matters: Instrumenting Success Like an) Tj T*
(A/B Experiment) Tj T*
(Before you can improve your agent, you must define what "better" means in the context of) Tj T*
(your business. Frame your observability strategy like an A/B test and ask yourself: what are) Tj T*
(the Key Performance Indicators \(KPIs\) that prove the agent is delivering value? These metrics) Tj T*
(should go beyond technical correctness and measure real-world impact: goal completion) Tj T*
(rates, user satisfaction scores, task latency, operational cost per interaction, and--most) Tj T*
(importantly--the impact on business goals like revenue, conversion or customer retention.) Tj T*
(This top-down view will guide the rest of your testing, puts you on the path to metrics driven) Tj T*
(development, and will let you calculate a return on investment.) Tj T*
(Quality Instead of Pass/Fail: Using a LM Judge) Tj T*
(Business metrics don't tell you if the agent is behaving correctly. Since a simple pass/fail is) Tj T*
(impossible, we shift to evaluating for quality using an "LM as Judge." This involves using a) Tj T*
(powerful model to assess the agent's output against a predefined rubric: Did it give the right) Tj T*
(answer? Was the response factually grounded? Did it follow instructions? This automated) Tj T*
(evaluation, run against a golden dataset of prompts, provides a consistent measure) Tj T*
(of quality.) Tj T*
(Creating the evaluation datasets--which include the ideal \(or "golden"\) questions and correct) Tj T*
(responses--can be a tedious process. To build these, you should sample scenarios from) Tj T*
(existing production or development interactions with the agent. The dataset must cover the) Tj T*
(full breadth of use cases that you expect your users to engage with, plus a few unexpected) Tj T*
(ones. While investment in evaluation pays off quickly, evaluation results should always be) Tj T*
(reviewed by a domain expert before being accepted as valid. Increasingly, the curation and) Tj T*
(maintenance of these evaluations is becoming a key responsibility for Product Managers) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
