(32) Tj T*
(Agents and Humans) Tj T*
(The most common form of agent-human interaction is through a user interface. In its) Tj T*
(simplest form, this is a chatbot, where a user types a request and the agent, acting as a) Tj T*
(backend service, processes it and returns a block of text. More advanced agents can provide) Tj T*
(structured data, like JSON, to power rich, dynamic front-end experiences. Human in the) Tj T*
(loop \(HITL\) interaction patterns include intent refinement, goal expansion, confirmation, and) Tj T*
(clarification requests.) Tj T*
(Computer use is a category of tool where the LM takes control of a user interface, often with) Tj T*
(human interaction and oversight. A computer use enabled agent can decide that the next) Tj T*
(best action is to navigate to a new page, highlight a specific button, or pre-fill a form with) Tj T*
(relevant information27.) Tj T*
(Instead of an agent using an interface on behalf of the user, the LM can change the UI to) Tj T*
(meet the needs of the moment. This can be done with Tools which control UI \(MCP UI\)28, or) Tj T*
(specialized UI messaging systems which can sync client state with an agent \(AG UI\)29, and) Tj T*
(even generation of bespoke interfaces \(A2UI\)30. These dynamic interactions are now natively) Tj T*
(supported via the Agent-to-UI protocol \(A2UI\) in the Gemini Enterprise app, allowing) Tj T*
(custom agents to dynamically generate rich, native UI components,like interactive data) Tj T*
(visualizations and structured forms,directly within the user's workspace.) Tj T*
(Of course, human interaction is not limited to screens and keyboards. Advanced agents are) Tj T*
(breaking the text barrier and moving into real-time, multimodal communication with "live) Tj T*
(mode" creating a more natural, human-like connection. Technologies like the Gemini Live) Tj T*
(API31 enable bidirectional streaming, allowing a user to speak to an agent and interrupt it, just) Tj T*
(as they would in a natural conversation.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
