(34) Tj T*
(protocol is the final piece of the puzzle, enabling the collaborative, Level 3 multi-agent) Tj T*
(systems that represent the frontier of automation. A2A transforms a collection of isolated) Tj T*
(agents into a true, interoperable ecosystem.) Tj T*
(Agents and Money) Tj T*
(As AI agents do more tasks for us, a few of those tasks involve buying or selling, negotiating) Tj T*
(or facilitating transactions. The current web is built for humans clicking "buy," the) Tj T*
(responsibility is on the human. If an autonomous agent clicks "buy" it creates a crisis of) Tj T*
(trust - if something goes wrong, who is at fault? These are complex issues of authorization,) Tj T*
(authenticity, and accountability. To unlock a true agentic economy, we need new standards) Tj T*
(that allow agents to transact securely and reliably on behalf of their users.) Tj T*
(This emerging area is far from established, but two key protocols are paving the way. The) Tj T*
(Agent Payments Protocol \(AP2\) is an open protocol designed to be the definitive language) Tj T*
(for agentic commerce. It extends protocols like A2A by introducing cryptographically-signed) Tj T*
(digital "mandates." These act as verifiable proof of user intent, creating a non-repudiable) Tj T*
(audit trail for every transaction. This allows an agent to securely browse, negotiate, and) Tj T*
(transact on a global scale based on delegated authority from the user. Complementing this) Tj T*
(is x402, an open internet payment protocol that uses the standard HTTP 402 "Payment) Tj T*
(Required" status code. It enables frictionless, machine-to-machine micropayments, allowing) Tj T*
(an agent to pay for things like API access or digital content on a pay-per-use basis without) Tj T*
(needing complex accounts or subscriptions. Together, these protocols are building the) Tj T*
(foundational trust layer for the agentic web.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
