(Page 40 of 54 - 01 - Introduction  to Agents) Tj T*
(Introduction to Agents) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(40) Tj T*
(Scaling Up from a Single Agent to an Enterprise Fleet) Tj T*
(The production success of a single AI agent is a triumph. Scaling to a fleet of hundreds) Tj T*
(is a challenge of architecture. If you are building one or two agents, your concerns are) Tj T*
(primarily about security. If you are building many agents, you must design systems to handle) Tj T*
(much more. Just like API sprawl, when agents and tools proliferate across an organization,) Tj T*
(they create a new, complex network of interactions, data flows, and potential security) Tj T*
(vulnerabilities. Managing this complexity requires a higher-order governance layer integrating) Tj T*
(all your identities and policies and reporting into a central control plane.) Tj T*
(Security and Privacy: Hardening the Agentic Frontier) Tj T*
(An enterprise-grade platform must address the unique security and privacy challenges) Tj T*
(inherent to generative AI, even when only a single agent is running. The agent itself becomes) Tj T*
(a new attack vector. Malicious actors can attempt prompt injection to hijack the agent's) Tj T*
(instructions, or data poisoning to corrupt the information it uses for training or RAG.) Tj T*
(Furthermore, a poorly constrained agent could inadvertently leak sensitive customer data or) Tj T*
(proprietary information in its responses.) Tj T*
(A robust platform provides a defense-in-depth strategy to mitigate these risks. It starts with) Tj T*
(the data, ensuring that an enterprise's proprietary information is never used to train base) Tj T*
(models and is protected by controls like VPC Service Controls. It requires input and output) Tj T*
(filtering, acting like a firewall for prompts and responses. Finally, the platform must offer) Tj T*
(contractual protections like intellectual property indemnity for both the training data and the) Tj T*
(generated output, giving enterprises the legal and technical confidence they need to deploy) Tj T*
(agents in production.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
