(Page 41 of 54 - 01 - Introduction  to Agents) Tj T*
(Introduction to Agents) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(41) Tj T*
(Agent Governance: A Control Plane instead of Sprawl) Tj T*
(As agents and their tools proliferate across an organization, they create a new, complex) Tj T*
(network of interactions and potential vulnerabilities, a challenge often called "agent sprawl.") Tj T*
(Managing this requires moving beyond securing individual agents to implementing a higher-) Tj T*
(order architectural approach: a central gateway that serves as a control plane for all) Tj T*
(agentic activity.) Tj T*
(Imagine a bustling metropolis with thousands of autonomous vehicles--users, agents, and) Tj T*
(tools--all moving with purpose. Without traffic lights, license plates and a central control) Tj T*
(system, chaos would reign. The gateway approach creates that control system, establishing) Tj T*
(a mandatory entry point for all agentic traffic, including user-to-agent prompts or UI) Tj T*
(interactions, agent-to-tool calls \(via MCP\), agent-to-agent collaborations \(via A2A\), and direct) Tj T*
(inference requests to LMs. By sitting at this critical intersection, an organization can inspect,) Tj T*
(route, monitor, and manage every interaction.) Tj T*
(This control plane serves two primary, interconnected functions:) Tj T*
(1. Runtime Policy Enforcement: This control plane is operationalized via the new Agent) Tj T*
(Gateway, which enforces consistent security policies across any environment. It acts) Tj T*
(as the architectural chokepoint for implementing security. It handles authentication \("Do) Tj T*
(I know who this actor is?"\) and authorization \("Do they have permission to do this?"\).) Tj T*
(Centralizing enforcement provides a "single pane of glass" for observability, creating) Tj T*
(common logs, metrics, and traces for every transaction. This transforms the spaghetti of) Tj T*
(disparate agents and workflows into a transparent and auditable system.) Tj T*
(2. Centralized Governance: To enforce policies effectively, the gateway needs a source) Tj T*
(of truth. This is provided by a central registry--an enterprise app store for agents and) Tj T*
(tools. This registry allows developers to discover and reuse existing assets, preventing) Tj T*
(redundant work, while giving administrators a complete inventory. More importantly,) Tj T*
ET
endstream
