(Page 43 of 54 - 01 - Introduction  to Agents) Tj T*
(Introduction to Agents) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(43) Tj T*
(How agents evolve and learn) Tj T*
(Agents deployed in the real world operate in dynamic environments where policies,) Tj T*
(technologies, and data formats are constantly changing. Without the ability to adapt,) Tj T*
(an agent's performance will degrade over time--a process often called "aging"--leading) Tj T*
(to a loss of utility and trust. Manually updating a large fleet of agents to keep pace with) Tj T*
(these changes is uneconomical and slow. A more scalable solution is to design agents) Tj T*
(that can learn and evolve autonomously, improving their quality on the job with minimal) Tj T*
(engineering effort.43) Tj T*
(How agents learn and self evolve) Tj T*
(Much like humans, agents learn from experience and external signals. This learning process is) Tj T*
(fueled by several sources of information:) Tj T*
(* Runtime Experience: Agents learn from runtime artifacts such as session logs,) Tj T*
(traces, and memory, which capture successes, failures, tool interactions, and decision) Tj T*
(trajectories. Crucially, this includes Human-in-the-Loop \(HITL\) feedback, which provides) Tj T*
(authoritative corrections and guidance.) Tj T*
(* External Signals: Learning is also driven by new external documents, such as updated) Tj T*
(enterprise policies, public regulatory guidelines, or critiques from other agents.) Tj T*
(This information is then used to optimize the agent's future behavior. Instead of simply) Tj T*
(summarizing past interactions, advanced systems create generalizable artifacts to guide) Tj T*
(future tasks. The most successful adaptation techniques fall into two categories:) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
91 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 2 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 612 792] /Contents 92 0 R /Resources << /Font << /F1 3 0 R >> >> >>
endobj
92 0 obj
<< /Length 1950 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
36 756 Td
13 TL
(Page 44 of 54 - 01 - Introduction  to Agents) Tj T*
(Introduction to Agents) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(44) Tj T*
(* Enhanced Context Engineering: The system continuously refines its prompts, few-) Tj T*
(shot examples, and the information it retrieves from memory. By optimizing the context) Tj T*
(provided to the LM for each task, it increases the likelihood of success.) Tj T*
(* Tool Optimization and Creation: The agent's reasoning can identify gaps in its) Tj T*
(capabilities and act to fill them. This can involve gaining access to a new tool, creating a) Tj T*
(new one on the fly \(e.g., a Python script\), or modifying an existing tool \(e.g., updating an) Tj T*
(API schema\).) Tj T*
(Additional optimization techniques, such as dynamically reconfiguring multi-agent design) Tj T*
(patterns or using Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback \(RLHF\), are active areas) Tj T*
(of research.) Tj T*
(Example: Learning New Compliance Guidelines) Tj T*
(Consider an enterprise agent operating in a heavily regulated industry like finance or life) Tj T*
(sciences. Its task is to generate reports that must comply with privacy and regulatory rules) Tj T*
(\(e.g., GDPR\).) Tj T*
(This can be implemented using a multi-agent workflow:) Tj T*
(1. A Querying Agent retrieves raw data in response to a user request.) Tj T*
(2. A Reporting Agent synthesizes this data into a draft report.) Tj T*
(3. A Critiquing Agent, armed with known compliance guidelines, reviews the report. If it) Tj T*
(encounters ambiguity or requires final sign-off, it escalates to a human domain expert.) Tj T*
(4. A Learning Agent observes the entire interaction, paying special attention to the) Tj T*
(corrective feedback from the human expert. It then generalizes this feedback into a new,) Tj T*
(reusable guideline \(e.g., an updated rule for the critiquing agent or refined context for the) Tj T*
(reporting agent\).) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
93 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 2 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 612 792] /Contents 94 0 R /Resources << /Font << /F1 3 0 R >> >> >>
endobj
94 0 obj
<< /Length 684 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
36 756 Td
13 TL
(Page 45 of 54 - 01 - Introduction  to Agents) Tj T*
(Introduction to Agents) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(45) Tj T*
(Figure 7: Sample multi agent workflow for compliance guidelines) Tj T*
(For instance, if a human expert flags that certain household statistics must be anonymized,) Tj T*
(the Learning Agent records this correction. The next time a similar report is generated,) Tj T*
(the Critiquing Agent will automatically apply this new rule, reducing the need for human) Tj T*
(intervention. This loop of critique, human feedback, and generalization allows the system to) Tj T*
(autonomously adapt to evolving compliance requirements44.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
95 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 2 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 612 792] /Contents 96 0 R /Resources << /Font << /F1 3 0 R >> >> >>
endobj
96 0 obj
<< /Length 2017 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
36 756 Td
13 TL
(Page 46 of 54 - 01 - Introduction  to Agents) Tj T*
(Introduction to Agents) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(46) Tj T*
(Simulation and Agent Gym - the next frontier) Tj T*
(The design pattern we presented can be categorized as in-line learning, where agents) Tj T*
(need to learn with the resources and design pattern they were engineered with. More) Tj T*
(advanced approaches are now being researched, where there is a dedicated platform that is) Tj T*
(engineered to optimize the multi-agent system in offline processes with advanced tooling and) Tj T*
(capabilities, which are not part of the multi-agent run-time environment. The key attributes of) Tj T*
(such an Agent Gym45 are:) Tj T*
(1. It is not in the execution path. It is a standalone off-production platform, and therefore can) Tj T*
(have the assistance of any LM model, and offline tools, cloud application and more) Tj T*
(2. It offers a simulation environment, so the agent can 'exercise' on new data and learn. This) Tj T*
(simulation environment is excellent for 'trial-and-error' with many optimizations pathways) Tj T*
(3. It can call advance synthetic data generators, which guide the simulation to be as real as) Tj T*
(possible, and pressure test the agent \(this can include advance techniques, such as red-) Tj T*
(teaming, dynamic evaluation and a family of critiquing agents\)) Tj T*
(4. The arsenal of the optimization tools is not fixed, and it can adopt new tools \(either) Tj T*
(through open protocols such as MCP or A2A\), or in a more advanced setting - learn new) Tj T*
(concepts and craft tools around them) Tj T*
(5. Finally, even constructs such as Agent Gym, may not be able to overcome certain edge-) Tj T*
(case \(due to the well known problem of 'tribal knowledge' in the enterprise\). In those cases) Tj T*
(we see the Agent Gym able to connect to the human fabric of domain experts, and consult) Tj T*
(with them on the right set of outcomes to guide the next set of optimizations) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
